  «text (500,4380) 1 7 1 0x1000000 -1 -1 "ï»¿source stage (OUTH pin)"Â»
  «text (500,2180) 1 7 1 0x1000000 -1 -1 "ï»¿sink stage (OUTL pin)"Â»
  «text (500,4800) 1.3 7 1 0x1000000 -1 -1 "ï»¿TOP FET DRIVER (1ED3140)"Â»
  «text (500,-1220) 1 7 1 0x1000000 -1 -1 "ï»¿source stage (OUTH pin)"Â»
  «text (500,-3420) 1 7 1 0x1000000 -1 -1 "ï»¿sink stage (OUTL pin)"Â»
  «text (500,-800) 1.3 7 1 0x1000000 -1 -1 "ï»¿BOTTOM FET DRIVER (1ED3140)"Â»
  «text (-3600,6700) 1.6 7 1 0x1000000 -1 -1 "ï»¿HALF-BRIDGE GATE DRIVER (hierarchical sheet, one per half bridge)"Â»
  «text (-3600,6350) 1 7 1 0x1000000 -1 -1 "ï»¿One 1ED3140 per FET, each drawn as two stages: a source stage (OUTH pin) and a sink stage (OUTL pin)."Â»
  «text (-3600,6150) 1 7 1 0x1000000 -1 -1 "ï»¿A stage switches on only while its IN+ is high and its IN- is low."Â»
  «text (-3600,5950) 1 7 1 0x1000000 -1 -1 "ï»¿IN- carries the other FET's PWM: that is the 1ED3140 interlock against cross conduction."Â»
  «text (-3600,5750) 1 7 1 0x1000000 -1 -1 "ï»¿Ports (the six flagged labels): PWM_H and PWM_L are 3.3 V logic from the controller, which sets the dead time."Â»
  «text (-3600,5550) 1 7 1 0x1000000 -1 -1 "ï»¿G_T / S_T go to the top FET gate and source, G_B / S_B to the bottom FET."Â»
  «text (-3600,5350) 1 7 1 0x1000000 -1 -1 "ï»¿V_T and V_B are ideal 12 V supplies floating on the FET source. EN pins are tied to the supply."Â»
»
